From de22df22228592971a7e3523fe57b5b4f3d45a91 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marius S <39998+winding-lines@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:27:07 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] Make the 100 MB response limit a per-client setting;
 don't cap streams

HttpClient.max_response_bytes (default MAX_RESPONSE_BYTES, 100 MB) is
the largest body a request buffers. get_stream does not buffer, so it no
longer refuses a Content-Length over the limit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
